{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter and Sally Plan a Road Trip", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Home Run", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people and places in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of people and places in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.  You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was      happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: The last time I was here, I <span class=\"strong\">watched</span> an incredible game. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: The crowd was <span class=\"strong\">cheering</span> when Boston won that big game!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>.</br> Irregular verbs change in different ways.</br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by  the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you as \u2026 ?</span></br> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Past Continuous, we add <span class = \"italic\">was/were + verb -ing</span> to verbs. Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add <span class = \"italic\"> -ing</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am/is/are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"--------\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"watch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"watched\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were watching\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"jump\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"jumped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were jumping\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"root\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rooted\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were rooting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were hitting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"try\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tried\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were trying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spill\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spilled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were spilling\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Baseball", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Every sport has specific language and terms for the place, the equipment and the game.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Let's look at the following terms for baseball.</br><span class = \"bullet\">baseball park: the stadium or park where the game is played</span></br><span class = \"bullet\">bat: a large wooden stick used to hit the ball</span></br><span class = \"bullet\">glove: a large leather glove used to catch the ball</span></br><span class = \"bullet\">inning: one round in which each team gets a turn to bat the ball and score while the other team catches</span></br><span class = \"bullet\">base: 3 separate squares around the field that a player must run to and touch with his foot</span></br><span class = \"bullet\">home run: when a player hits a ball hard and has enough time to run around all 3 bases back to the home plate</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the next Toronto <span class = \"italic\"><span class = \"strong\">batter</span></span> hits a <span class = \"strong\">home run</span>, then all 4 players will score.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cheer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to help a team or player do better by shouting positive comments", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter lost his voice because he cheered a lot for his team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a baseball game.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "absolutely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "completely or totally", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter absolutely cheers for the whole game.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to root for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cheer on your team", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have to root for our team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "home run", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when a player hits a ball, then runs around the bases to score a point", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bases are loaded now, so I hope this batter hits a home run.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tense", "type": "name"}, {"content": "nervous or not able to relax", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All the fans are tense because it's the last inning and the scores are so close.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "batter", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the player on the team who comes up to bat (hit the ball)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If this batter hits a home run, we will get at least one point.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to load (the bases)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put a player on all 3 of the bases ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When the bases were loaded, the batter tried to hit a home run.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "The championship for American Major League Baseball is called the World Series. Do research on last year's World Series champion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find information to answer the following questions: <ul><li>What team was the champion last year?</li><li>Who was the other team?</li><li>What was the winning score in the series? ___ Games - ___ Games</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write sentences to answer the above questions. Be sure to use the Past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your knowledge with your partner by reading your sentences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I do research on Major League Baseball.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I locate speci